e us will make good on its  promises and become a leader in the  fight against global warming  could president biden declare a climate  emergency  that's what the senate's top democrat  chuck schumer is calling for  it's a controversial move allowing the  president to bypass  congress on certain issues and funnel  money to clean energy projects  everyone is fixated on the price of  bitcoin but one thing they often don't  think about  is its impact on the environment  according to digi economists the kryptos  carbon footprint is about 37  million tons that's about the same as  new zealand a country of five  million people and elon musk is offering  a 100  million dollar prize for the best carbon  capture technology  the world's richest man wants to find  ways to lower the cost  and use the emissions to make rocket  fuel carbon capture can be used to trap  greenhouse gases from  plants and factories or even directly  from the air  i'm jennifer zabasaja in new york kaylee  after eight years of back and forth  president biden canceled the keystone xl  oil pipeline project  within hours of assuming office the only  problem  construction on the pipeline was already  underway  now the citizens of oye and alberta have  to make new plans for the community  bloomberg's robert tuttle visited the  small town to investigate  it's empty there's absolutely no one  here the  keystone xl pipeline is empty pipe just  lying around here  [Music]  i'm visiting you from oyen alberta  and until a few days ago this was kind  of ground zero for construction of the  keystone xl pipeline that all pretty  much came to a halt a few days ago when  joe biden  on his first day in office as u.s  president signed an executive order that  rescinded a  permit that was given by the previous  administration to build the pipeline  fairly recently as many as a thousand  people  just staying here working on this oil  pipeline  i did not expect to see that in the  first hundred days  i had a guy born with me and he comes in  at 10 o'clock  and he says hey i'm done he left i think  there's still 300  guys left you know they didn't all just  exit town just like that  you know they can't leave the pipe  exposed so they're going to close that  up they'll be done here in a month  people are still holding on to the hope  that the project isn't dead  you're still kind of hopeful that maybe  this project can be revived do you think  uh yeah we're we're waiting for news  from transcanada and we're just  we'll just go forward until we not hear  those news but it's clear  that many of the workforce here are  getting ready to leave or have left  keystone xl was a very controversial  pipeline it was going to be built to  carry  as much as 800 000 barrels a day of oil  sands crewed from alberta  down into the united states its critics  claimed that it would contribute to  global warming by fostering development  of the oil sands  but the industry oil industry here said  that they needed that pipeline to  deliver their oil to market  this town has kind of been waiting to  see what happens  uh  [Music]  for more on this let's bring in our  resident green expert hotshot  rati akshat the cancellation of this  project led to job losses that doesn't  help the economic recovery that we need  could you put that into context for us  that's certainly right we know that tc  energy  has laid out about 1000 jobs connected  to the project  and in this environment any job losses  aren't welcome but there's a bigger  story here  and the environmentalists argue that  it's not just about one pipeline  the goal is to try and wean the entire  society of fossil fuels  so yes in any transition you will have  some job losses  but what's coming in the form of green  energy  and what could be a green recovery will  create  many times more jobs and put out fewer  emissions  why is it fossil fuel pipelines that  have become such a hot button issue what  do they mean specifically for climate  change  yeah it'